witness and brought a film crew to document

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:26.300
what he saw. The result is an impressive new
documentary called slava Ukraine, meaning

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:33.300
glory to Ukraine. It is out now in select
theaters Benard Henri levy, thank you.

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:37.120
&gt;&gt; Thank you.
&gt;&gt; I want to ask you about the issue of bravery.

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:44.840
It is struck me as sometimes underrated when
you think about we think about smarts and

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:51.739
intelligence and but if you think of great
leadership, like with zelenskyy, bravery,

00:00:51.739 --> 00:00:54.039
courage is one of the most important things.

00:00:54.039 --> 00:00:55.039
[10:40:07 AM]

00:00:55.039 --> 00:00:57.399
things. Do you think that is trained? Do you
think it is in-born?

00:00:57.399 --> 00:01:04.619
&gt;&gt; It is one of the most important and one
of the most forgotten. We were so surprised

00:01:04.619 --> 00:01:11.400
when zelenskyy decided to stay. We were so
surprised when the whole Ukrainian people

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:22.040
stood at his side. It was absolutely unexpected.
None of us thought that. But they have -- but

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:34.310
nevertheless, it happened. We have brave citizenship
like in the beginning of America, like in

00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:40.320
Athens in the ancient Greece, like in the
French revolution. This is what happened many

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:46.130
Ukraine. And this is one of the great events
which we saw.

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:50.869
&gt;&gt; When you went on the front lines and you
talked to these soldiers, they're up against

00:01:50.869 --> 00:01:56.560
are very formidable foe and the Russias are
hammering and they're doing things that are

00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:57.560
[10:41:08 AM]

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:00.180
